  "worked_solution": "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $2+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(2+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{8\\text{i}}{2+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8\\text{i}(2-2\\text{i})}{(2+2\\text{i})(2-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{16\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{2}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{16+16\\text{i}}{8} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $2=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=2$ and $q=2.$",
